Refuse startup if another instance is running
==============================================

If you try to start a second instance of the application, it will refuse to start and display an error message. This is to prevent conflicts and ensure that only one instance of the application is running at a time.
To check if another instance is running, the application uses a lock file. When the application starts, it creates a lock file in a specific location. If the lock file already exists, it means that another instance of the application is running, and the new instance will display an error message and exit.
If you want to allow multiple instances of the application to run simultaneously, you can disable this feature by modifying the application's settings. However, it is generally recommended to keep this feature enabled to avoid potential issues with data corruption or conflicts between instances.
